From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:11:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Don't pause the player of a media element that is
 potentially playing

update_media_state() asks the player to play when the media element is
potentially playing and the player is paused, and otherwise pauses a
playing player. So it also paused the player when the element was
potentially playing and the player was playing already: play() on a
playing element paused the media while `paused` stayed false, and so
did a change of the ready state while playing. This came with
servo/servo#41027, which made the method skip requests that don't
change the state of the player.

Pause the player only when the element is not potentially playing.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: a new test, playing-the-media-resource/play-while-playing.html, which times out without this patch.

Validation: host release builds (`./mach build --release`) of ohos-main and of ohos-main with this patch and the three that follow it, a muted `<video>` playing movie_5.mp4 that calls play() again 1.5 s after the first play(): without the patches, `currentTime` went from 1.00 to 1.40 in the next 2 s and stayed there; with them, to 3.00. A HiHope DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0, API 26) with headless release builds (`./mach build --ohos --release --headless-binary`): from 1.19 to 1.19 without, from 1.01 to 3.02 with. For the WPT runs, see the next patch.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; found and fixed by the agent during review rework)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
